{"name":"creator-matrix-colour-choice","manifest":{"title":"Colour Choice","description":"An offline visual app for choosing red, green, or blue and showing the selected colour.","operations":[{"name":"ask","description":"Choose a colour and see its label in the same surface."}],"settings":[],"slots":[],"icon":null,"toolbar":null,"entry":{"kind":"surface","name":"notes"}},"spec":"# Colour Choice

This app is an offline visual surface with a colour selector and a text note showing the selected colour.

## Domain rules

- The app must use only installed contracts and must not use a network connection or runtime AI.
- The selector must offer exactly these values and labels: `red` with label `Red`, `green` with label `Green`, and `blue` with label `Blue`.
- The selected value and the text note must always correspond to the same colour.
- The app must not apply explicit styling.

## Surface composition

When the app is installed or opened, compose the declared `notes` surface idempotently from the installed contracts. The surface contains one select control and one text note. Opening reads the current state only and never runs colour-selection domain work.

## Initial colour

**When** the surface has no initialized colour state.

**Then** initialize the selected value to `red` and set the text note to `Red`.

**Afterwards** the select control shows `Red` as selected, the text note shows only `Red`, and the state is marked initialized.

## Choose a colour

**When** the person chooses a value in the select control.

**Then** store the chosen value and update the text note in the same `notes` surface to that value's label: `Red`, `Green`, or `Blue`.

**Afterwards** the select control and text note are visibly updated together, with the note showing only the selected colour's label.","files":{"helpers.cs":"using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Select;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter;
public static class ColourChoice
{
    public static readonly IReadOnlyList<SelectOption> Options = new[] { new SelectOption("red", "Red"), new SelectOption("green", "Green"), new SelectOption("blue", "Blue") };
    public static string Label(string value) => value == "green" ? "Green" : value == "blue" ? "Blue" : "Red";
}","compose.cs":"using DigitalBrain.Apps;
using DigitalBrain.Apps.Signals;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Surface;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Select;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Text;
await using var brain = await DigitalBrainClient.ConnectAsync(args);
var app = brain.Get<IApp>(brain.Setting("App")!);
var root = brain.Setting("App")!;
var surface = brain.Get<ISurface>(root + "/notes");
var select = brain.Get<ISelect>(root + "/colour");
var note = brain.Get<IText>(root + "/note");
await select.Set("Colour", ColourChoice.Options, "red");
var text = await note.Read();
if (text.Version == 0) await note.Set("Red");
await surface.Set(new SurfaceDefinition("Colour choice", new[] { new UiChildRef(UIVocabulary.SelectType, root + "/colour"), new UiChildRef(UIVocabulary.TextType, root + "/note") }), 0);
await foreach (var request in brain.On<AppRequested>(app, brain.Stopping)) { }","choose.cs":"using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Select;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Text;
await using var brain = await DigitalBrainClient.ConnectAsync(args);
var root = brain.Setting("App")!;
var select = brain.Get<ISelect>(root + "/colour");
var note = brain.Get<IText>(root + "/note");
await foreach (var changed in brain.On<SelectChanged>(select, brain.Stopping))
{
    await select.Set("Colour", ColourChoice.Options, changed.Value);
    await note.Set(ColourChoice.Label(changed.Value));
